    "Block",
    {
      "type_": "variable",
      "labels": [ [ "Lit", "ssl_profiles" ] ],
      "body": [
        [
          "Attribute",
          "description",
          [
            "Heredoc",
            [
              "EOF",
              "\nA map of SSL profiles.\n\nSSL profiles can be later on referenced in HTTPS listeners by providing a name of the profile in the `name` property.\nFor possible values check the: `ssl_policy_type`, `ssl_policy_min_protocol_version` and `ssl_policy_cipher_suites` properties\nas SSL profile is a named SSL policy - same properties apply.\nThe only difference is that you cannot name an SSL policy inside an SSL profile.\n\nEvery SSL profile contains following attributes:\n\n- `name`                            - (`string`, required) name of the SSL profile.\n- `ssl_policy_name`                 - (`string`, optional, defaults to `null`) name of predefined policy.\n- `ssl_policy_min_protocol_version` - (`string`, optional, defaults to `null`) the minimal TLS version.\n- `ssl_policy_cipher_suites`        - (`list`, optional, defaults to `null`) a list of accepted cipher suites.\n"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [ "Attribute", "default", [ "Object", [] ] ],
        [ "Attribute", "nullable", [ "Bool", false ] ],
        [
          "Attribute",
          "type",
